  "query_preview": "..\nA dry pattern will remain over the Marianas through tonight. To the\nnorth, Invest 93W was downgraded to medium by the Joint Typhoon \nWarning Center (JTWC), and is expected to move northeast to east- \nnortheast. As 93W progresses, convection to the west of the Marianas\nlooks to progress eastward, increasing POPs (Probability of \nPrecipitation) across the Marianas. This batch of showers is \nexpected to move through over the weekend, with a brief dry period \nreturning for Monday. Then, Invest 92W, currently north of Kosrae, is\nexpected to approach the region. As of now, most of the models agree\nthat Invest 92W will move through as only a weak disturbance, or \npossibly a weak tropical depression, with only the GFS and ECMWF \ndeterministic models showing a stronger system. Therefore, it looks \nlike a wetter pattern is in store for the Marianas Tuesday through \nmost of the week, with gusty winds in showers. Invest 92W will \ncontinue to be monitored closely for any changes to expected \ndevelopment.",
